      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add 5–10 at.% W to TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "W atoms will remain in the BCC matrix and produce solid-solution strengthening and lattice distortion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding W will favorably alter the electronic bonding state of TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12623424::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bonding-state depletion is correlated with plastic-strain behavior in BCC high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12623424::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "W has a high melting point and strong bonding characteristics.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12623424::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "W-induced lattice distortion will increase lattice resistance and pin dislocations at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "W-induced dislocation pinning will improve high-temperature strength retention.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 5–10 at.% W will increase the 1273 K yield and compressive strengths of TiVNbTa by roughly 10–20%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The W-modified alloy will retain acceptable ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved high-temperature strength without excessive ductility loss will make the alloy better suited to W-to-CuCrZr heat-transfer service.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
